    "https://uog.peopleadmin.com/postings/5458": {
      "title": "Extension Associate II",
      "description": "University of Guam Applicant Portal | Extension Associate II Skip to Main Content Employment Portal Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UOG HRO Home Position Specifications EEO/ADA & Title IX Office Inadahi yan Inagofli’e Contact Us Extension Associate II Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. THE UNIVERSITY OF GUAM SOLICITS APPLICATIONS TO ESTABLISH A LIST OF ELIGIBLES FOR THE FOLLOWING LIMITED TERM APPOINTMENT, FEDERALLY FUNDED FULL-TIME POSITION (SUBJECT TO THE AVAILABILITY OF FUNDS): Please apply at http://uog.peopleadmin.com University of Guam is a drug-free work environment and an equal opportunity employer, military family, disability and veterans are encouraged to apply. Federal Law requires presentation of proof of identity and eligibility to work in the U.S. We comply with this law on a nondiscriminatory basis. For technical assistance or inquiries in completing the application, please contact Eliza Soriano at esoriano@triton.uog.edu Applicants claiming degrees or credit hours are required to have an original or copy of the documents (e.g., transcripts, high school diploma) or GED certification accompany the application. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Extension Associate II Posting Number 080-26 Full or Part Time Full Time Work Schedule Monday to Friday, 8:00am to 5:00pm Position End Date 09/18/2026 Salary Range UGPP /M-01 $49,731.00 – UGPP /M-18 $87,650.00 Job Description Summary Under the supervision of the Land Grant Extension faculty, the Extension Associate II will implement and evaluate theextension programs; develop recruitment and educational material to promote and reinforce Extension and grant objectives;draft program reports; collect, manage, and analyze data; document success stories/program impacts; participate in,evaluate, and improve extension-based learning activities and outreach events; and create and foster relationships with community partners that will support the Extension mission. The Extension Associate II will work independently after abrief training in following specific procedures to which assigned, primarily supporting the Extension and grant objectives.This position requires intra-island travel – and may include off-island travel – and high level of communication skill (oral andwritten) in working with participants, community partners and stakeholders, and secondary target audiences. Duties include,but are not limited to, creating and maintaining partnerships; coordinating, implementing, and reporting project activities ina timely manner; executing project work plans; assisting in managing project operations and extension activities; assistingwith team member supervision; managing data and writing reports; and other detailed projects as assigned in accordancewith stated grant objectives. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree with 5 years relevant and related work experience, or Master’s Degree with no related work experience. Preferred Qualifications Master’s Degree in Nutrition, Health & Wellness or related field; at least,1 year experience in Extension and Outreach, CITI Certification Minimum Knowledge, Abilities and Skills Must have excellent communication skills both oral and written; demonstrate the ability to work independently within the scope of project and/or supervisor directives; have a good understanding of the components of grants and some experience with grant or report writing; have knowledge in nutrition and health, lifestyle behaviors to manage and/or prevent non communicable diseases; have organizational and management skills to coordinate community-based programming; have knowledge of the community and cultures of the residents of Guam; have the ability to navigate Guam villages independently or with simplified directions; have the ability to be flexible and adjust schedule to meet the community’s needs; proficient in Microsoft Office suite and educational material software/media (e.g. Canva, Instagram) and have experience in and comfortable with public speaking. Physical Requirements Other Information Job Open Date 09/04/2026 Job Application Deadline 09/18/2026 Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants THE UNIVERSITY OF GUAM SOLICITS APPLICATIONS TO ESTABLISH A LIST OF ELIGIBLES FOR THE FOLLOWING LIMITED TERM APPOINTMENT , FEDERALLY FUNDED FULL - TIME POSITION ( SUBJECT TO THE AVAILABILITY OF FUNDS ): Please apply at http://uog.peopleadmin.com University of Guam is a drug-free work environment and an equal opportunity employer, military family, disability and veterans are encouraged to apply. Federal Law requires presentation of proof of identity and eligibility to work in the U.S. We comply with this law on a nondiscriminatory basis. For technical assistance or inquiries in completing the application, please contact Eliza Soriano at esoriano@triton.uog.edu Applicants claiming degrees or credit hours are required to have an original or copy of the documents (e.g., transcripts, high school diploma) or GED certification accompany the application. Additional Information Contact Information For further inquiries you may contact the University of Guam Human Resources Office at (671)735-2350 or email at uoghro@triton.uog.edu Application Process Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * * Do you meet the minimum education as stated in the job announcement? Bachelor's Degree with 5 years relevant and related work experience, or Master's Degree with no related work experience. Yes No * Do you meet the necessary special qualification as stated in the job announcement? Must have a valid driver's license. Yes No * Do you meet the preferred qualifications as stated in the job announcement? Master's Degree in Nutrition, Health & Wellness or related field; at least 1 year experience in Extension and Outreach, CITI Certification Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Driver's License Bachelor's Transcript Optional Documents Up-to-date Curriculum Vitae or Resume Unofficial Transcripts Master's Transcript Unibetsedȧt Guåhan UOG Station Mangilao, Guam 96913 Campus Map To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
